Its central research question is:

"Can an integrated reliability-auditing framework identify unreliable diabetes-risk predictions and infeasible explanations more effectively than conventional evaluation based primarily on predictive performance and feature importance?"

The framework must evaluate five dimensions:

1. Predictive performance.
2. Probability calibration and prediction uncertainty.
3. Explanation stability and counterfactual feasibility.
4. Subgroup fairness and reliability.
5. Generalization under dataset shift.

Build an experimental pipeline that compares a conventional baseline system against the proposed RiskTrust framework.

Do not assume the proposed framework will outperform the baseline. Measure the results and report positive, negative, or inconclusive findings honestly.

